===Etymology 1===
From {{der|en|NL.|saccharum|t=sugar}} + [[w:English language|English]] {{m|en|-ine|pos={{glossary|suffix}} meaning ‘of or pertaining to’ forming {{glossary|adjective}}s}}.<ref>{{R:Lexico|pos=adj|nodot=1}}; compare {{R:OED Online|pos=adj.'' and ''n.|id=169420|date=1909}}</ref> {{m|la||Saccharum}} is derived from {{m|la|saccharon|t=syrupy liquid from bamboo or reeds}}, from {{der|en|grc|σάκχαρον}}, from {{der|en|pi|sakkharā|t=sugar; gravel; granule, grain; crystal; potsherd}}, from {{der|en|sa|शर्करा|tr=śárkarā|t=ground or candied sugar; cotton sugar, sugarmaple; gravel, grit, pebbles; potsherd}}, ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*ḱorkeh₂|t=boulder; gravel}}.

====Adjective====
{{en-adj}}

# {{lb|en|dated}} Of or relating to [[sugar#Noun|sugar]]; [[sugary]].
#: {{synonyms|en|saccharous|q1=archaic, rare}}
# {{lb|en|dated}} [[contain|Containing]] a [[large]] or [[excessive]] [[amount#Noun|amount]] of sugar.
#: {{synonyms|en|cloying|sickly|sickly sweet}}
# {{lb|en|figurative|derogatory}} [[excessively|Excessively]] [[sweet#Adjective|sweet]] in [[action#Noun|action]] or [[disposition]], especially if [[romantic#Adjective|romantic]] or [[sentimental]] to the [[point#Noun|point]] of [[ridiculousness]]; [[sickly sweet]], [[syrupy]].
#: {{synonyms|en|cloying|precious|saccharined|sickly|twee}}
#: {{antonyms|en|nonsaccharine}}
# {{lb|en|chiefly|botany|geology}} [[resemble|Resembling]] [[granulated#Adjective|granulated]] sugar; [[saccharoid]].

